Cell["\<\
Symbolical multiplication is much slower and produces large output. After \
substitution both answers coincide. Below we provide basis examples  how \
noncommutative elements behaves with various products when gaFieldProduct is \
set to CommutativeProduct. Note that for all operations (OuterProduct, \
InnerProduct, etc) field elements are multiplied by CommutativeProduct\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9690706088236322`*^9, 3.969070662742538*^9}, {
